// tests/test_vocab_adpcm.c - IMA-ADPCM decoder and clip pack (spec 8.5; AC-35, AC-36; A6).
//
// Always (CI included, no clip pack needed):
// - AC-35: main/vocab_adpcm.c is bit-exact with the reference decoder adpcm_step() in
//   tools/vocab_audio/build_clips.py: fixed vectors generated by that reference (predictor
//   and step index after every code, including predictor clamping at +32767/-32768, index
//   clamping at 0 and 88 and a corrupt state index), packed-nibble decoding at odd/even
//   code offsets in any chunk size.
// - The pack parser main/vocab_clips.c (format in main/vocab_clips.h): a reference pack whose
//   bytes are pinned here AND in tests/test_vocab_clips.py (so the C parser and the Python
//   writer agree), every malformed variant rejected with its status (and installed as "no
//   clips"), 20,000 random mutations and truncations parsed without reading outside the
//   blob, the installed-pack lookups, and the committed empty fallback
//   (assets/audio/vocab_clips_empty.bin): count 0, every bank uid -> NULL.
// Only when the local, git-ignored pack exists ($VOCAB_CLIPS_DIR, default assets/audio):
// - AC-36 on the real pack: sorted unique uids, 4-byte aligned, inside the blob, every bank
//   uid resolves, unknown uids -> NULL; AC-35 on real data: every clip decoded by the C
//   decoder hashes to the pcm_sha256 that the reference decoder wrote into the manifest.
//   Without the pack a skip notice is printed (CI and public checkouts have no word audio).
//
// Runs from the repository root (tools/validate.sh). VOCAB_CLIPS_EMPTY overrides the path of
// the empty fallback. Compiled with:
//   tests/test_vocab_adpcm.c main/vocab_adpcm.c main/vocab_clips.c
//   main/vocab_bank.c main/vocab_rng.c main/vocab_view.c
